e and Operations Assistant provides administrative support to the Western Indiana Workforce Development Board. Primary responsibilities include assisting with accounts payable documentation, obtaining and organizing vendor bids and quotes, tracking purchases and invoices, maintaining records, preparing meeting materials, and supporting other routine office operations. This posi... View Details Bookmark Math Tutor ST2600153 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The Math Tutor will be responsible for providing one-on-one math tutoring with elementary age children. View Details Bookmark Reading Tutor ST2600152 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The Reading Tutor will be responsible for providing one-on-one tutoring with elementary age children. View Details Bookmark Ryves Youth Center Recreation Assistant ST2600151 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No Recreation Assistants help with all facets of recreation at Ryves Youth Center. View Details Bookmark Student Media Digital Photographer ST2600177 Student Media 08/31/2026 09/30/2026 No The photographers report directly to the Student Digital Media Manager and take photos for various departments and colleges on campus. They are responsible for collecting data and maintaining a database of all human subjects of the photographs taken. View Details Bookmark Terre Haute Children's Museum Before & After-school Program Assistant ST2600162 Off-Campus Work Study 08/24/2026 09/24/2026 No Assist with implementing before and/or after-school programs at Deming Early Learning Center, 1750 8th Ave. Terre Haute, IN. View Details Bookmark United Way Administrative Assistant ST2600170 University Controller 08/22/2026 09/22/2026 No The Administrative Assistant serves as the welcoming first point of contact for the organization and provides essential administrative support to staff, community partners, volunteers, and visitors. This position is responsible for maintaining an organized and professional front office, handling incoming communications, assisting with routine administrative tasks, and supporting the day-to-day ... View Details Bookmark CASY After School Youth Assistant ST2600169 University Controller 08/22/2026 09/22/2026 No The Chances and Services for Youth after School Youth Assistant will work with paid and volunteer staff to provide quality services and care of children who attend the after-school program located at 1101 S 13th St, Terre Haute, IN 47802. View Details Bookmark CASA Student Office Assistant and Social Media Ambassador ST2600149 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The CASA Student Office Assistant and Social Media Ambassador will assist with social media content creation, event flier creation and assistance, marketing and recruitment assistance, and general office duties. View Details Bookmark Swope Art Museum Gallery Assistant ST2600155 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No Gallery Assistants serve as the first public contact for the Swope Art Museum and play a vital role in maintaining the Museum’s welcoming, safe, and professional environment. Gallery Assistants are responsible for the comfort and safety of Museum patrons, the security of exhibited works of art, and providing support for the Museum’s day-to-day operations. View Details Bookmark Swope Art Museum Maintenance Assistant ST2600154 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The Maintenance Assistant supports the Sheldon Swope Art Museum in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for visitors, staff, and the Museum’s collection. Working under the direction of the Swope’s Facilities Manager, the Maintenance Assistant performs routine cleaning and maintenance tasks throughout the Museum and assists with other facilities-related needs as assigned. View Details Bookmark CASA Student Office Assistant ST2600148 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The CASA Student Office Assistant will assist with front desk tasks including filing, data entry, and assisting office staff and visitors. They will also assist with dockets and report distribution as well as calling people in to court. View Details Bookmark Brownstone Manor Custodial Maintenance Technician ST2600147 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The Custodial Maintenance Technician provides floor care, dusting, restroom upkeep and waste management at Brownstone Manor Senior Apartments. View Details Bookmark Brownstone Manor Resident Services Assistant ST2600146 University Controller 08/19/2026 09/19/2026 No The Resident Services Assistant assists with resident activities including games, fitness classes and social events. They also assist with administrative office tasks and promotion and advertising of activities to the residents. View Details Bookmark CANDLES Social Media Coordinator ST2600121 University Controller 08/15/2026 09/15/2026 No Generating educational content and distributing it through the museum’s social media channels, as well as, responding to individuals through these same channels. View Details Bookmark CANDLES Museum Services Assistant ST2600120 University Controller 08/15/2026 09/15/2026 No Employee will assist coordinators in operations of the museum.  Museum Service Assistants are a resource for our guests and staff. View Details Bookmark Off-Campus Work Study: Camp Navigate After School Mentor ST2600123 Off-Campus Work Study 08/15/2026 09/15/2026 No A Camp Navigate After School Mentor (Counselor) is responsible for leading, implementing, and assisting with the planning of all programs and experiences for children in small and large group settings. They will be responsible for the general safety and development, growth, and skill achievement of the participants in his/her group. Mentors will provide high quality educational and recreational... View Details Bookmark United Campus Ministries Student Assistant ST2600079 University Controller 08/12/2026 09/12/2026 No Student will work with Campus Minister and Office Manager to perform daily tasks and operate the Student Food Pantry. View Details Bookmark Terre Haute Children's Museum Program Assistant ST2600050 Off-Campus Work Study 08/06/2026 09/06/2026 No Assist with implementing education department events. View Details Bookmark 14th & Chestnut Community Center After-School Youth Assistant ST2600049 Off-Campus Work Study 08/06/2026 09/06/2026 No Will include leading kids through different activities. These activities include helping with homework, playing games, leading crafts, supervising on playground and occasional field trips, as well as leading different discussions and various activities. View Details Bookmark To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
